import lib/process.dl

function the process test interpreter:
    execute:
        return "python" if the process platform is Windows, else "python3"

set discovery to a process command for the process test interpreter
add "-c" as an argument to discovery
add "import sys; sys.stdout.write(sys.executable)" as an argument to discovery
run discovery and set found to it
set interpreter to found's standard output

print whether found succeeded as a line

set command to a process command for interpreter
add "-c" as an argument to command
add "import os,sys; data=sys.stdin.read(); ascii_case=os.environ.get('DYNLEX_MIXED_CASE') == 'third' and os.environ.get('dynlex_mixed_case') == ('third' if os.name == 'nt' else 'second'); unicode_case=os.environ.get('DYNLEX_Ä') == 'third' and os.environ.get('dynlex_ä') == ('third' if os.name == 'nt' else 'second'); print(sys.argv[1] + '|' + data + '|' + os.path.basename(os.getcwd()) + '|' + os.environ['DYNLEX_PROCESS_VALUE'] + '|' + str(os.environ.get('PATH') == 'dynlex-overridden-path') + '|' + str('DYNLEX_REMOVED' in os.environ) + '|' + str(sys.argv[2] == '') + '|' + str(sys.argv[3] == 'trailing' + chr(92)) + '|' + str(ascii_case) + '|' + str(unicode_case)); print('separate error', file=sys.stderr); sys.exit(7)" as an argument to command
add "literal $HOME ; * \"quoted\"" as an argument to command
add "" as an argument to command
set trailing to a new string buffer containing 9 bytes
copy (the string form of "trailing") into the data of trailing at offset 0
store 92 as a byte into the data of trailing at 8
add trailing as an argument to command
use "tests/required/process_run" as the working directory of command
set environment variable "DYNLEX_PROCESS_VALUE" of command to "overridden"
set environment variable "PATH" of command to "dynlex-overridden-path"
set environment variable "DYNLEX_MIXED_CASE" of command to "first"
set environment variable "dynlex_mixed_case" of command to "second"
set environment variable "DYNLEX_MIXED_CASE" of command to "third"
set environment variable "DYNLEX_Ä" of command to "first"
set environment variable "dynlex_ä" of command to "second"
set environment variable "DYNLEX_Ä" of command to "third"
set environment variable "DYNLEX_REMOVED" of command to "temporary"
unset environment variable "DYNLEX_REMOVED" of command
run command using (the string form of "standard input") and set result to it

print whether result was launched as a line
print whether result succeeded as a line
print result's exit code as a line
print whether (result's standard output = "literal $HOME ; * \"quoted\"|standard input|process_run|overridden|True|False|True|True|True|True\n") as a line
print whether (result's standard error = "separate error\n") as a line
print whether (result's error message = "") as a line

set unset to a process command for interpreter
add "-c" as an argument to unset
add "import os; print('PATH' in os.environ)" as an argument to unset
unset environment variable "PATH" of unset
run unset and set cleared to it

print whether cleared succeeded as a line
print whether (cleared's standard output = "False\n") as a line

set isolated to a process command for interpreter
add "-c" as an argument to isolated
add "import os; print(os.environ.get('DYNLEX_ONLY', 'missing') + '|' + str('PATH' in os.environ))" as an argument to isolated
do not inherit the environment in isolated
set environment variable "DYNLEX_ONLY" of isolated to "present"
run isolated and set separation to it

print whether separation succeeded as a line
print whether (separation's standard output = "present|False\n") as a line
